   126	### 1.5 The gates before it replaces the running pipeline
   127	
   128	The new system replaces the running pipeline only after it passes five gates, in order (D548, written by the council under D439;
   129	D544):
   130	
   131	| Gate | Its lines, and whose | Where it stands |
   132	|---|---|---|
   133	| 1. The ladder step (Stage A) | Alex's six lines (D400): no question other than the topic's; no part left unlisted; no outcome with no range or with two; no unjustified decline; 35 of 44 topics right in two of three sends, 28 of them with written answer choices; the same favourable end in all three sends and the same due day for nine in ten. | Not passed; missed in all nine readings. |
   134	| 2. The judge on the system's own questions (Stage B) | D428: unsupported figure answers at most five points above the baseline; unsupported yes/no answers at most 5%; unsupported last answers at most 3 in 30; enough controls. | Not passed: 4 comparable controls against 8 needed; the strictest last-answer reading missed (3 of 24). |
   135	| 3. End to end against the running pipeline | D427, D431: both systems, unseeded, the same day, three draws each, on the frozen ruler, with Step 2's three lines checked in the same run. | Owed. "Beats" is not yet defined in numbers. |
   136	| 4. Use on unseen news | Opened by Alex beside the others (D484). Its lines (four in five big matters covered; at most one in five questions trivial or duplicate; nine in ten last answers supported; at most one in twenty cited statements wrong; no undelivered fact that would change an answer) are proposed, not his. | Not an accepted gate yet. |
   137	| 5. Integration and release | The whole path on production storage and the product's pages, accepted on the product's own path. | Partly built: the product page and API read a store of the new system (D570–D573); the live-store contract is agreed for test stores only (D593). |
